node_modules/
# `out/*` and not `out/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# negation under one can never take effect. Written as `out/` for months, the
# `!out/samples/` below did nothing and the sample videos — the whole deliverable
# — were silently absent from the repository. They only ever appeared because an
# early commit force-added them; the moment the seeds changed and the filenames
# with them, they stopped being committed and nobody was told.
out/*
# ...except the sample videos, which are the deliverable.
!out/samples/
# ...and the ability demo, which is how the ten new ones get reviewed at all:
# seven of them are movement, and movement does not survive a screenshot.
!out/demo/
# ...but never the frame scratch. A render writes one PNG per frame beside the
# mp4 and removes them when the encode succeeds; interrupt it and 200MB of
# stills stay behind, inside the one directory the rules above re-include.
out/samples/.frames/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vitest/
dist/
tmp/

# Generated audio assets (see src/export/audio.ts)
assets/audio/*.wav

# Чужие ролики: см. refs/videos/README.md
refs/videos/*.mp4
